y\nassert v._selection_key(viewport)==key  # narrowed: scalar generation excluded\n```\n_projected_selection_index needs `self._host.framebuffer_size()` and camera — initialize_state sets camera. Also `_visibility_state` — set in initialize_state presumably. And `_projected_selection_index` iterates display entries needing entry fields (owners, hit_elements etc.) — add_mesh_arrays creates them.\n\nTest: after scalar update, `v._selection_index is not None` still (not cleared by _mesh_changed since change=='scalar') and `_selection_key(viewport) == v._selection_index_key` → index reused. Then `handle.update_positions(new)` → key differs → rebuild. Also `handle.set_transform(...)` → differs. And camera change → differs.\n\nE. Tk compatibility: scheduler without notifier — covered in test_scheduler (no notifier → submit works, drain works).\n\nNow — one important check: `_projected_selection_index` — does it depend on `entry[\"handle\"].generations` indirectly? It uses `_selection_key` for caching only. Fine.\n\nAlso — does anything else use `_selection_index_key` comparisons where the narrowed key could wrongly match? `_mesh_changed` sets `_selection_index=None` for non-scalar changes; scalar changes keep index. With narrowed key, scalar change → key unchanged → cached index reused. Correct per design.\n\nWait — one more: `_selection_key` includes `entry[\"handle\"].visible` and `removed` and `deformation_scale`. Appearance generation (set_visible bumps 'appearance') — visible separately keyed. update_appearance (scalar_range/colormap) bumps 'appearance' — not in narrowed key → no rebuild. Correct: colors don't affect geometry index.\n\nHmm — but wait: does the projected index include preselected/highlight coloring? No — geometry/visibility/ownership only.\n\nNow, before writing tests, double-check `_show_animation_frame` reuse path against `_apply_highlight_masks` — it calls `self.make_current()`? In retained_viewer `_apply_highlight_masks` — does it call make_current? In qt.py there's a wrapper `_apply_highlight_masks` that calls make_current then super. The base RetainedViewer._apply_highlight_masks — let me check it doesn't need host stuff beyond renderer. It was called in old code path too. Fine.\n\nAlso `v._show_animation_frame(0)` directly — the qt.py wrapper calls make_current; base method fine with fake host.\n\nOne more potential issue: `capture_animation_frame` iterates `self._entries` — requires entries with \"appearance\" etc. — fine.\n\n`begin_animation_cache` calls `stop_animation` → `_restore_live_renderer` → iterates `_animation_handles` (empty) and re-adds live entries to renderer (already added) — `_SoftwareResources.add_mesh` just overwrites appearance dict. Fine.\n\nLet me now check `_display_entries` and `_apply_highlight_masks` quickly for required entry keys, and check what `initialize_state` sets for `_visibility_state`.", "summary": []}
